                <pb facs="0590" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5484: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-20T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:46
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>137. Department’s telegram No. 74, March 19, 6 p.m. General McCoy and I recommend
                    that Colonel Francis Le J. Parker be designated at once as alternate to General
                    McCoy on the National Board of Elections.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
